  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMUNZI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMUNZI is a collaborative project between three partners: International Medical Cooperation Committee (IMCC), United Children of Africa (UNICA) and Zimbabwe Medical Students? Association (ZiMSA). Since 2014, the IMUNZI project has worked towards lowering the HIV/AIDS prevalence in Zimbabwe among youth. In its modified form, it has become a double-pronged project that still emphasizes on HIV awareness, but also focuses on mental health disorders related to HIV with the view of improving the health of youth in Zimbabwe. While continuing with peer to peer education, boot camps, sports tournaments and workshops, the partners will work with relevant authorities to strengthen their partnership and work towards a common goal.</narrative>
  </description>
